# Chapter 3 Activity requests. Start the app first: dotnet run (https://localhost:7001, Development).
# A browser address bar sends only GET requests, so send these POST requests and headers from here.
# Each "Expect" line is the status you should see. Every response, from both route families, carries
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff and X-Frame-Options: DENY.

@host = https://localhost:7001

###
# The main path without the exercise identity. Expect 401
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Idempotency-Key: order-1001

###
# The main path with the local test identity. Expect 200 {"key":"order-1001"}
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Idempotency-Key: order-1001
X-Exercise-Identity: developer

###
# The mock webhook branch needs no exercise identity. Expect 200 {"key":"hook-2001"}
POST {{host}}/webhooks/demo
Idempotency-Key: hook-2001

###
# A missing key fails before any route runs. Expect 400
POST {{host}}/api/payments
X-Exercise-Identity: developer

###
# An invalid key (a space and "!" are not allowed). Expect 400
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Idempotency-Key: bad key!
X-Exercise-Identity: developer

###
# The branch accepts only POST /webhooks/demo. Expect 404
GET {{host}}/webhooks/demo
